;PALASM Design Description
; pds2v test: purely combinatorial address decoder.
; Exercises STRING macros, multi-line equations, active-low left sides,
; XOR/XNOR, VCC/GND, an output enable (.TRST) and a read-back of an output.
; EXPECT-EXIT: 0
; EXPECT: warning: SPARE (pin 13) is never used

TITLE    pds2v test decoder
PATTERN  decoder
REVISION 1
AUTHOR   test
COMPANY  none
DATE     1995-10-01
CHIP     DEC  MACH111

PIN  4   AS_N                     ; dedicated inputs
PIN  26  RW
PIN  40  A31
PIN  41  A30
PIN  42  A29
PIN  43  A28
PIN  44  FC2
PIN  1   FC1
PIN  13  SPARE
PIN  2   ROM_N      COMBINATORIAL
PIN  3   RAM_N      COMBINATORIAL
PIN  8   IO_N       COMBINATORIAL
PIN  9   ANY_N      COMBINATORIAL ; reads back ROM_N, RAM_N, IO_N
PIN  10  PAR        COMBINATORIAL ; A31 xor A30 xor A29 xor A28
PIN  11  SAME       COMBINATORIAL ; A31 xnor A30
PIN  18  HI         COMBINATORIAL ; constant 1
PIN  19  LO         COMBINATORIAL ; constant 0
PIN  20  DOUT       COMBINATORIAL ; three-state, enabled on read
PIN  21  OE_N       COMBINATORIAL

STRING  CYC    '( /AS_N * FC2 )'
STRING  ROMSEL '/A31 * /A30'

EQUATIONS
/ROM_N = CYC * ROMSEL           ; active low: ROM_N = NOT(...)
/RAM_N = CYC * /A31 * A30
       + CYC * A31 * /A30 * /A29
/IO_N  = CYC
       * A31 * A30 * A29        ; continuation over several lines
ANY_N  = ROM_N * RAM_N * IO_N
PAR    = (A31 :+: A30) :+: (A29 :+: A28)
SAME   = A31 :*: A30
HI     = VCC
LO     = GND
DOUT   = FC1
DOUT.TRST = RW * /AS_N
OE_N   = /( RW * /AS_N )
